From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 101/101] PC5: a game's own web browser processes are helpers, not
 handed off (Wine patch 0995)

World of Tanks starts its Chromium Embedded Framework browser,
cef_browser_process.exe, as its hangar loads. Its name was none of the
helpers', so it was handed off: the game ended and the title started the
browser in its place, which then failed to hand off cef_subprocess.exe.
A program whose name has "cef_" in it is now a helper: its start fails,
and the game goes on.
---
 docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md                             |  2 +-
 ...dll-ps5-a-crash-handler-is-not-handed-off.patch | 14 ++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
index a129023..e69cb83 100644
--- a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
+++ b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ before evaluating a candidate built from that cache.
 | 0992 | `win32u`: on PS5, a USB keyboard's keys, which the console sends by their place as a US keyboard names them (input type 7, `PW_WINE_INPUT_KEYBOARD_KEY`), are sent as the keys of the layout `WINE_PS5_KEYBOARD` names (`gb`, `fr`, `ca`, `de`, `es`, `latam`, `it`, `pt`, `br`, `dk`, `no`, `se`, `fi`, `pl`, `cz`, `hu`, `ro`, `tr`, `ru`, `ua`, `gr`; PC5 sets it from the console's language) with that layout's characters, through a `KBDTABLES` (`pKbdLayerDescriptor`) built from `dlls/win32u/ps5kbd.h`, which `tools/make_ps5_keyboards.py` writes from xkeyboard-config. AltGr is Ctrl+Alt as on Windows, and Alt+Shift switches a Cyrillic or Greek layout with US. Unset or `us`, the keyboard is the US one as before, and the keys the controller's button mapping names (type 1) keep their US places under any layout. The log says `wine-ps5: keyboard layout NAME`. A French AZERTY keyboard typed as QWERTY, with no way to type @ (World of Tanks' login). |
 | 0993 | `server` (Leo Lobato's prospero-win): on PS5, read-only regular files past a budget of 48 cached and about 48 live descriptors are parked (closed, the least recently used first) and opened again by name when needed, with their position, as 0871 does for directories: a title can open only about 250 files however high `RLIMIT_NOFILE` is, and games that keep hundreds of archives open failed with "Too many open files". `WINE_PS5_PARK_FILES`, `WINE_PS5_CACHED_FILES` |
 | 0994 | `server`: on PS5, a parked folder (0871) or read-only file (0993) opened again by its name whose device or inode number changed (a file system that numbers files anew at each open) is taken instead of failing with `STATUS_FILE_DELETED`; that and every failure to open one again is logged (`wine-ps5: parked …`, eight times at most each) |
-| 0995 | `ntdll`: a program whose name has `handler` or `errormonitor` (World of Tanks' `WargamingErrorMonitor.exe`) in it, or whose command line has `--database=`, `crashpad` or `--url=` in it (in any case), is a helper for the PS5 title's hand-off (`PW_HANDOFF`), as a crash reporter is: it isn't handed off, its start fails, and the game that started it carries on. Mina the Hollower starts its crash handler, `handler.exe --database=…\Crashpad … --url=https://submit.backtrace.io/…`, at boot; it was handed off, so the game ended |
+| 0995 | `ntdll`: a program whose name has `handler`, `errormonitor` (World of Tanks' `WargamingErrorMonitor.exe`) or `cef_` (the Chromium Embedded Framework's processes, World of Tanks' hangar: `cef_browser_process.exe`, `cef_subprocess.exe`) in it, or whose command line has `--database=`, `crashpad` or `--url=` in it (in any case), is a helper for the PS5 title's hand-off (`PW_HANDOFF`), as a crash reporter is: it isn't handed off, its start fails, and the game that started it carries on. Mina the Hollower starts its crash handler, `handler.exe --database=…\Crashpad … --url=https://submit.backtrace.io/…`, at boot; it was handed off, so the game ended |
 | 0996 | `server`: on PS5, a `create_file`, rename or hard link with a root folder and an absolute unix name (what 0943 gives when it looks a name up by the folder's own name) is taken instead of failing with `STATUS_OBJECT_PATH_SYNTAX_BAD`: the unix name is opened as it is and the NT name is still made from the folder's. Heroes of Might and Magic: Olden Era got "path invalid" (`ERROR_BAD_PATHNAME`) for `StreamingAssets\maps\Story_maps` right after 0943's log line |
 | 0997 | `kernelbase`: on PS5, the listing 0988 writes for `fxc.exe` gives a `def` line's values as plain decimals (`1.0`, `-0.5`, `0.333333343`; vkd3d-shader writes `1.00000000e+00`, and `D3DXAssembleShader` takes no exponent), and a `vs_1_x` shader that fails to compile (vkd3d-shader's `E7002` for `sincos`) is compiled for `vs_2_0` instead, as Far Cry only assembles the listing again on a device that takes `vs_3_0` |
 | 0998 | `ntdll`: on PS5, a non-alertable `NtWaitForSingleObject` on an event or semaphore whose one try on the shared word (0885, 0887) fails spins up to `WINE_PS5_SYNC_SPIN_US` microseconds (100 by default, 0 off, 1000 at most; never longer than a relative timeout, none for a poll or an absolute time) re-trying the word before it blocks in the server, and stops at once when the server holds the word. While it spins the word stays the client's, so `SetEvent`/`ReleaseSemaphore` need no server call either. Blur sets six events about 2000 times a frame, each waking a worker that waits again, and each of those waits and sets cost several microseconds through the server (5 to 10 ms a frame). The log says `wine-ps5: waits spin up to N us before blocking` at the first such wait, and every 65536 spins how many took the object (`wine-ps5: wait spins: …`); `tests/test_wine_sync_spin.py` runs the spin on the actual word header |
diff --git a/wine/patches/0995-ntdll-ps5-a-crash-handler-is-not-handed-off.patch b/wine/patches/0995-ntdll-ps5-a-crash-handler-is-not-handed-off.patch
index 6d3bb67..13b8cc1 100644
--- a/wine/patches/0995-ntdll-ps5-a-crash-handler-is-not-handed-off.patch
+++ b/wine/patches/0995-ntdll-ps5-a-crash-handler-is-not-handed-off.patch
@@ -13,7 +13,10 @@ A program whose name has "handler" in it, or whose command line has
 "--database=", "crashpad" or "--url=" in it (in any case), is now a
 helper: its start fails as other helpers' do, and the game goes on.
 So is one whose name has "errormonitor" in it: World of Tanks starts
-WargamingErrorMonitor.exe, its crash reporter, as it boots. The name
+WargamingErrorMonitor.exe, its crash reporter, as it boots. And one
+whose name has "cef_" in it: World of Tanks draws its hangar with the
+Chromium Embedded Framework, whose cef_browser_process.exe it starts as
+the hangar loads; handed off, the game ended there. The name
 is also taken after the last forward slash, so a folder in a path
 written with them is not read as part of the name.
 ---
@@ -36,7 +39,7 @@ index 3eee653..b9d2f36 100644
  static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struct pe_image_info *pe_info )
  {
      static const char * const helpers[] =
-@@ -706,7 +706,15 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
+@@ -706,7 +706,18 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
          /* A game that starts its settings tool and waits for it (Far Cry, FarCryConfigurator.exe
           * /Caller=FarCry) goes on to the game when that start fails. */
          "config", "setting",
@@ -45,6 +48,9 @@ index 3eee653..b9d2f36 100644
 +        "handler",
 +        /* World of Tanks' WargamingErrorMonitor.exe, its crash reporter */
 +        "errormonitor",
++        /* the Chromium Embedded Framework's own processes, a game's menus drawn as web pages
++         * (World of Tanks' hangar: cef_browser_process.exe, then cef_subprocess.exe) */
++        "cef_",
      };
 +    /* the same crash handler told by its command line, whatever its name: Crashpad's
 +     * database and the address its reports are sent to */
@@ -52,7 +58,7 @@ index 3eee653..b9d2f36 100644
      const char *file = getenv( "PW_HANDOFF" ), *dir = getenv( "PW_HANDOFF_DIR" ), *name;
      char image[1024], current[1024], command[4096], cwd[1024], lower[256], text[6200];
      size_t i;
-@@ -719,6 +727,7 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
+@@ -719,6 +730,7 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
      if (!image[0] || !strcasecmp( image, current ) || strncasecmp( image, dir, strlen( dir ))) return;
      name = strrchr( image, '\\' );
      name = name ? name + 1 : image;
@@ -60,7 +66,7 @@ index 3eee653..b9d2f36 100644
      for (i = 0; name[i] && i < sizeof(lower) - 1; i++) lower[i] = (name[i] >= 'A' && name[i] <= 'Z') ? name[i] + 32 : name[i];
      lower[i] = 0;
      for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(helpers); i++)
-@@ -728,6 +737,16 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
+@@ -728,6 +740,16 @@ static void ps5_hand_off( const RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS *params, const struc
          return;
      }
      ps5_utf8( &params->CommandLine, command, sizeof(command) );
